  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="cf7e52eb-0a52-4995-814f-dec2788ebc45" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e1f655a9-5546-46d4-81b3-34e1ab3db3b0" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3">
    <problem>
      <para>For each equation in questions 1 – 5, identify the values of \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) that you would substitute into the quadratic formula to solve the equation.</para>
      <para>\(3x^2+8x+4=0\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?<para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(a=3\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
